Demonstrating Linux System Calls Using Kernel APIs.

Explanation:

Function - Purpose
open() - Opens or creates a file.
write() - Writes data into a file.
lseek() - Moves the file pointer.
read() - Reads data from a file.
getpid() - Returns the current process ID.
close() - Closes the file descriptor.


Important concepts:

File descriptor (fd): An integer returned by open() that identifies an opened file.
Kernel API: An interface through which a user-space program requests services from the Linux kernel.
System call: A mechanism used by programs to request operating-system services.
O_CREAT – Creates a file if it doesn't exist.
O_RDWR – Opens a file for reading and writing.
O_TRUNC – Clears existing file content.
